1. Install Docker on the Raspberry Pi

	1. Update your system:
		---> sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get upgrade
	2. Download the Docker installation script:
		---> curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com -o get-docker.sh
	3. Run the installation script:
	 	---> sudo sh get-docker.sh
	4. Add your user to the Docker group: This allows you to run Docker commands without sudo.
		---> sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
		---> newgrp docker                      --- 
	5. Verify Docker installation:
		---> docker run hello-world

2.  Install nvidia-container-toolkit (if applicable)
	
	While Raspberry Pi doesn't have an NVIDIA GPU, you may encounter issues if you try to use NVIDIA-specific images or features. However, for some scenarios, having the NVIDIA Container Toolkit might be helpful. According to NVIDIA Docs installing nvidia-container-toolkit is part of the prerequisites for DeepStream Docker containers.
	---> Refer to the official installation guide to determine if you need to install it based on your specific requirements.

3. Obtain DeepStream Docker Image

	1. NVIDIA NGC: NVIDIA provides DeepStream Docker images on NGC. You'll need an NGC account and API key to pull them.
	2. Log in to NGC registry:
		---> docker login nvcr.io
				Username: $oauthtoken (literally type this)
				Password: <your NGC API key>.  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

	3. Pull a DeepStream Docker image: Choose an appropriate image, for example:
		---> docker pull nvcr.io/nvidia/deepstream:7.1-triton-arm-sbsa

4. Configure and Run the DeepStream Container

	1.Create a project folder (optional but recommended):
		mkdir project
		cd project
		mkdir configs data
	2.Mount the project folder to the container: This allows you to store configuration files, models, and data outside 	the container for persistence.
		--> docker run --gpus all -it --rm -v <path_to_your_project_folder>:/opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/sources/project -w /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/sources/project nvcr.io/nvidia/deepstream:5.1-21.02-devel

		--> docker run --gpus all -it --rm -v /home/pi5/project:/opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/sources/project -w /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/sources/project nvcr.io/nvidia/deepstream:7.1-triton-arm-sbsa


				* Replace <path_to_your_project_folder> with the actual path to your project directory.



